const erpPanel = "<dialog id=\"erp-project-panel\" class=\"erp-panel\" aria-labelledby=\"erp-project-title\"><div class=\"erp-bar\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-erp-close>← Back to Projects</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-erp-close autofocus>× Close</button></div><div class=\"erp-content\"><p class=\"section-label\">ERP research</p><h2 id=\"erp-project-title\">The people behind ERP performance.</h2><p class=\"erp-subtitle\">Bachelor’s thesis · Industrial Management</p><p class=\"erp-lead\">My thesis explores what happens after an ERP system goes live: how employees make it part of their daily work, and how that use may relate to manufacturing performance.</p><p class=\"erp-question\">The system is installed. What helps people turn it into everyday value?</p><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">01</span>What I worked on</summary><p>I focused on ERP use after implementation in Uzbek manufacturing companies, connecting academic research with practical questions about everyday work.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">02</span>My contribution</summary><ul><li>Reviewed existing research on ERP use after launch.</li><li>Developed a research framework connecting everyday system use with operational performance.</li><li>Prepared a survey-based study design for employees who use ERP in their work.</li><li>Built the study around established questionnaire measures, with English and Uzbek versions to support local participation.</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">03</span>Why this matters</summary><p>Production, inventory and procurement teams depend on shared information. This study asks what supports consistent ERP use across everyday operations.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">04</span>Who could benefit</summary><ul><li>Manufacturing managers: better-informed decisions about employee support after launch.</li><li>Employees: greater attention to their everyday system experience.</li><li>Operations teams: insights that may help improve coordination and information reliability.</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">05</span>Skills demonstrated</summary><div class=\"tags\"><span>Research design</span><span>Critical analysis</span><span>Business process understanding</span><span>Academic communication</span></div></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">06</span>Academic guidance</summary><p><span>Supervisor</span><br><strong>Dr. Shazadi Rameen Arshad</strong></p><p><span>Research advice and guidance</span><br><strong>Professor Alisher Dedahanov</strong></p><p>New Uzbekistan University · 2026</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">07</span>A local perspective</summary><p>The study brings the experiences of ERP users in Uzbekistan into a wider discussion about digital transformation, with attention to local working practices.</p></details><div class=\"erp-benefit\"><h3>The intended benefit</h3><p>Help manufacturers understand how to turn an ERP investment into more effective everyday use, with the aim of improving coordination and operational performance.</p><p class=\"erp-status\">Research focus: study design and anticipated contributions. Operational benefits remain to be evaluated.</p></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control erp-back\" data-erp-close>← Back to Projects</button></div></dialog>";
const odooPanel = "<dialog id=\"odoo-erp-panel\" class=\"erp-panel\" aria-labelledby=\"odoo-erp-title\"><div class=\"erp-bar\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-odoo-erp-close>← Back to Projects</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-odoo-erp-close autofocus>× Close</button></div><div class=\"erp-content\"><p class=\"section-label\">ERP project · Odoo</p><h2 id=\"odoo-erp-title\">How an integrated ERP connects a business.</h2><p class=\"erp-subtitle\">Functional ERP learning · Business process perspective</p><p class=\"erp-lead\">This project documents my practical study of Odoo as an integrated ERP platform and how its modules support cross-functional business processes.</p><p class=\"erp-question\">How can one system connect customers, sales, purchasing, inventory, operations, finance and management?</p><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">01</span>What I am studying</summary><p>I am exploring Odoo from a functional and business-process perspective: how separate departments work inside one connected ERP environment rather than as isolated tools.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">02</span>End-to-end workflow</summary><p>Lead → Quotation → Sales Order → Purchase / Replenishment → Inventory → Delivery → Invoice → Payment → Accounting.</p><p>This workflow helps me understand how one business transaction can move across commercial, operational and financial functions.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">03</span>Core Odoo modules</summary><div class=\"tags\"><span>CRM</span><span>Sales</span><span>Purchase</span><span>Inventory</span><span>Accounting</span><span>Manufacturing / MRP</span><span>HR</span><span>Project</span><span>Website / eCommerce</span></div></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">04</span>Business value I am analyzing</summary><ul><li>Connected workflows across departments.</li><li>A shared source of operational and financial information.</li><li>Process automation and clearer hand-offs.</li><li>Reporting that links transactions with business performance.</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">05</span>Skills I am developing</summary><div class=\"tags\"><span>ERP process mapping</span><span>Business requirements</span><span>Cross-functional analysis</span><span>Workflow design</span><span>Data &amp; reporting</span></div></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">06</span>Odoo learning &amp; certification</summary><p>I have completed the Odoo Student Diploma. I am also studying Odoo’s broader functional ecosystem; the official Odoo Functional Certification is a separate, version-specific certification pathway.</p><p><a class=\"erp-control\" href=\"assets/odoo-student-diploma.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">View Odoo Student Diploma certificate ↗</a></p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">07</span>Official Odoo platform</summary><p>Odoo is a modular business software platform that brings multiple business functions into one integrated environment.</p><p><a class=\"erp-control\" href=\"https://www.odoo.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Visit the official Odoo website ↗</a></p></details><div class=\"erp-benefit\"><h3>Project objective</h3><p>Build a practical understanding of how ERP systems connect business processes, data and decision-making across an organization.</p><p class=\"erp-status\">Focus: functional ERP understanding, process integration and Odoo-based business workflows.</p></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control erp-back\" data-odoo-erp-close>← Back to Projects</button></div></dialog>";
const ciscoPanel = "<dialog id=\"cisco-data-panel\" class=\"erp-panel\" aria-labelledby=\"cisco-data-title\"><div class=\"erp-bar\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-cisco-close>← Back to Projects</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-cisco-close autofocus>× Close</button></div><div class=\"erp-content\"><p class=\"section-label\">Cisco Networking Academy</p><h2 id=\"cisco-data-title\">Introduction to Data Science</h2><p class=\"erp-subtitle\">Certificate of Course Completion · Beginner · 6 hours</p><p class=\"erp-lead\">This Cisco Networking Academy course introduced me to the foundations of data science, data analytics and data engineering, together with how artificial intelligence and machine learning use data to support decisions and predictions.</p><p class=\"erp-question\">How does raw data become information that supports better decisions?</p><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">01</span>What the course covers</summary><p>The course provides a foundation in data science and explains the relationship between data analytics, data engineering, data science, artificial intelligence and machine learning.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">02</span>Curriculum</summary><ul><li>Experience Analytics</li><li>Data Collection and Storage</li><li>Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning</li><li>Embarking on Your Career in Data Analytics</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">03</span>Learning format</summary><ul><li>Beginner level with no recommended prerequisites.</li><li>Approximately 6 hours of learning.</li><li>4 modules and 5 practice lab activities.</li><li>Videos, knowledge checks, module quizzes and a final exam.</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">04</span>Knowledge and skills</summary><ul><li>Understanding how data analytics supports data-driven decisions.</li><li>Recognizing structured, semi-structured and unstructured data.</li><li>Understanding data collection, storage and preparation for analysis.</li><li>Exploring the 5 Vs of Big Data: Volume, Velocity, Variety, Veracity and Value.</li><li>Understanding how AI and machine learning use data.</li><li>Distinguishing between data analyst, data engineer and data scientist roles.</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">05</span>Course recognition</summary><p>Cisco Networking Academy recognizes completion of the course. Cisco also offers a related digital badge; its published earning criteria list a 70% passing score on the comprehensive exam.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">06</span>Why it is relevant to my profile</summary><p>The course strengthens my foundation in data-driven decision-making and complements my work in business analytics, management and digital transformation.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">07</span>Certificate &amp; official course</summary><p><a class=\"erp-control\" href=\"assets/IntrotoDataScienceUpdate.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">View my Cisco certificate ↗</a></p><p><a class=\"erp-control\" href=\"https://www.netacad.com/courses/introduction-data-science?courseLang=en-US\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">View the official Cisco course ↗</a></p></details><div class=\"erp-benefit\"><h3>What this adds to my profile</h3><p>A structured foundation in data concepts, analytics, AI/ML and the data career landscape, supporting more informed use of data in business and management contexts.</p><p class=\"erp-status\">Cisco Networking Academy · Introduction to Data Science · Certificate completed in 2026.</p></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control erp-back\" data-cisco-close>← Back to Projects</button></div></dialog>";
const rbmPanel = "<dialog id=\"rbm-experience-panel\" class=\"erp-panel rbm-panel\" aria-labelledby=\"rbm-experience-title\"><div class=\"erp-bar\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-rbm-close>← Back to Projects</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-rbm-close autofocus>× Close</button></div><div class=\"erp-content rbm-content\"><p class=\"section-label\">International experience · RBM RISE Week</p><div class=\"rbm-hero-grid\"><div class=\"rbm-hero-copy\"><h2 id=\"rbm-experience-title\">RISE Week at HKUST (Guangzhou)</h2><p class=\"erp-subtitle\">College of Future Technology · January 2026</p><p class=\"erp-lead\">I joined the CFT RBM International Student Experience Week and explored how cross-disciplinary learning connects university research with emerging technology companies.</p><div class=\"rbm-facts\"><span>Guangzhou, China</span><span>University + industry visits</span><span>International Experience</span></div></div><div class=\"rbm-photo rbm-photo-cover\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"RISE Week photo\"><span>RBM RISE Week</span></div></div><p class=\"erp-question\">From cross-disciplinary learning to smart mobility, drones and autonomous driving.</p><div class=\"rbm-visit-grid\"><article class=\"rbm-visit-card\"><div class=\"rbm-photo rbm-photo-hkust\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"HKUST Guangzhou visit photo\"><span>HKUST (GZ)</span></div><div class=\"rbm-visit-copy\"><p class=\"rbm-kicker\">University visit</p><h3>HKUST (Guangzhou)</h3><p>During RISE Week, I attended lectures and visited laboratories at HKUST(GZ). The College of Future Technology uses cross-disciplinary, project-based learning to connect academic study with real-world challenges.</p><a class=\"rbm-source-link\" href=\"https://www.hkust-gz.edu.cn/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Official HKUST(GZ) website ↗</a></div></article><article class=\"rbm-visit-card\"><div class=\"rbm-photo rbm-photo-xpeng\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"XPeng visit photo\"><span>XPeng</span></div><div class=\"rbm-visit-copy\"><p class=\"rbm-kicker\">Technology visit</p><h3>XPeng</h3><p>XPeng is a Guangzhou-headquartered technology company focused on smart electric vehicles. The visit gave me a closer look at how mobility companies combine vehicle development with software, intelligent systems and R&amp;D.</p><a class=\"rbm-source-link\" href=\"https://www.xpeng.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Official XPeng website ↗</a></div></article><article class=\"rbm-visit-card\"><div class=\"rbm-photo rbm-photo-dji\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"DJI visit photo\"><span>DJI</span></div><div class=\"rbm-visit-copy\"><p class=\"rbm-kicker\">Technology visit</p><h3>DJI</h3><p>DJI develops drone, imaging and stabilization technologies used across creative and professional fields. The visit highlighted how advanced hardware and software can become practical tools for industries.</p><a class=\"rbm-source-link\" href=\"https://www.dji.com/company\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Official DJI website ↗</a></div></article><article class=\"rbm-visit-card\"><div class=\"rbm-photo rbm-photo-pony\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pony.ai visit photo\"><span>Pony.ai</span></div><div class=\"rbm-visit-copy\"><p class=\"rbm-kicker\">Technology visit</p><h3>Pony.ai</h3><p>Pony.ai develops autonomous-driving technology across Robotaxi, Robotruck and personally owned vehicle applications. The visit provided exposure to how self-driving systems are being developed toward real-world deployment.</p><a class=\"rbm-source-link\" href=\"https://pony.ai/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Official Pony.ai website ↗</a></div></article></div><div class=\"erp-benefit rbm-certificate\"><div><h3>Participation certificate</h3><p>The programme certificate remains available here as formal evidence of participation.</p></div><a class=\"erp-control\" href=\"assets/HKUST(GZ).pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">View participation certificate ↗</a></div><div class=\"erp-benefit rbm-reflection\"><h3>What the week added to my perspective</h3><p>The experience connected academic learning with technology companies working on mobility, drones and autonomy, strengthening my interest in innovation, digital transformation and cross-functional problem solving.</p><div class=\"tags\"><span>International learning</span><span>Technology exposure</span><span>University–industry connection</span></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control erp-back\" data-rbm-close>← Back to Projects</button></div></dialog>";
const industry4Panel = "<dialog id=\"industry4-project-panel\" class=\"erp-panel industry4-panel\" aria-labelledby=\"industry4-project-title\"><div class=\"erp-bar\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-industry4-close>← Back to Projects</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control\" data-industry4-close autofocus>× Close</button></div><div class=\"erp-content industry4-content\"><p class=\"section-label\">University group project · Industry 4.0</p><h2 id=\"industry4-project-title\">Real-Time Capacity Monitoring for Manufacturing</h2><p class=\"erp-subtitle\">IMGT430 · Spring 2026</p><p class=\"erp-lead\">A university team project exploring how real-time production data can help Sales make more realistic delivery commitments and help Operations identify capacity constraints earlier.</p><p class=\"erp-question\">How can a factory connect incoming orders, machine status and capacity decisions without replacing its existing equipment?</p><div class=\"industry4-flow\" aria-label=\"Project system flow\"><span>Customer orders</span><b>→</b><span>IoT machine data</span><b>→</b><span>Capacity engine</span><b>→</b><span>Shared dashboard</span></div><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">01</span>The problem we addressed</summary><p>Our team focused on a common disconnect between Sales and production operations: orders may be captured manually, Sales may not have current shop-floor capacity information, and bottlenecks can become visible only when deadlines are already close.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">02</span>Proposed solution</summary><ul><li>Centralize incoming customer orders instead of relying on repeated manual spreadsheet entry.</li><li>Use IoT retrofit sensors or existing machine data interfaces to detect whether equipment is running, stopped or idle.</li><li>Collect and clean machine data through an edge gateway before sending it to a shared data environment.</li><li>Use a capacity engine to combine order demand with available machine capacity and identify bottlenecks.</li><li>Give Sales and Operations access to the same live dashboard for delivery and capacity decisions.</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">03</span>Real company visit &amp; confidentiality</summary><p>The project was informed by an on-site visit to a real manufacturing company. We are grateful to the organization for allowing us to observe its operations and learn from a real production environment. At the company’s request, its name is not disclosed publicly. This portfolio therefore presents only the project concept, process observations and academic analysis, while respecting the company’s confidentiality preference.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">04</span>What makes the concept practical</summary><ul><li>Links customer-order information with production-capacity data instead of treating machine monitoring as a separate engineering dashboard.</li><li>Can work with older equipment through retrofit sensors such as vibration or current-draw monitoring.</li><li>Supports gradual rollout: begin with one production line, validate the concept, then expand.</li><li>Uses a lightweight digital representation of available capacity rather than requiring a full 3D digital twin.</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">05</span>Financial feasibility model</summary><p>As part of the academic project, our team developed an illustrative pilot business case for one production line. The model estimated an initial investment of about $120,000, a projected net annual benefit of about $68,000 and an estimated payback period of roughly 21 months.</p><div class=\"industry4-metrics\"><div><strong>~$120k</strong><span>Illustrative pilot investment</span></div><div><strong>~$68k</strong><span>Projected net annual benefit</span></div><div><strong>~21 mo.</strong><span>Estimated payback</span></div></div><p class=\"erp-status\">These figures are academic project estimates based on model assumptions; they are not audited results or disclosed financial data from the visited company.</p></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">06</span>Implementation approach</summary><ul><li>Phase 1: map the process, select a pilot line and define required data.</li><li>Phase 2: install sensors, configure the gateway and build the initial dashboard.</li><li>Phase 3: run the pilot with Sales and Operations feedback and refine the system.</li><li>Phase 4: expand to additional production lines and add forecasting or automated alerts.</li></ul></details><details class=\"erp-detail\"><summary><span class=\"erp-number\">07</span>Skills demonstrated</summary><div class=\"tags\"><span>Industry 4.0</span><span>IoT concepts</span><span>Process analysis</span><span>Capacity planning</span><span>Cost-benefit analysis</span><span>Sales &amp; Operations alignment</span><span>Team project work</span></div></details><div class=\"erp-benefit\"><h3>Project objective</h3><p>Bridge the information gap between customer commitments and production reality by giving Sales and Operations a shared, real-time view of capacity.</p><p class=\"erp-status\">University group project · conceptual system design and feasibility analysis · no report file is published on this website.</p></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"erp-control erp-back\" data-industry4-close>← Back to Projects</button></div></dialog>";
